<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodora Megale Komnene</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Theodora Komnene, Despina Khatun, Theodora of Trebizond</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Despina Khatun was the name borne by Theodora Komnene, daughter of Emperor John IV of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a>, who married the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aq-qoyunlu">Aq Qoyunlu</a> ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzun-hasan">Uzun Hasan</a> around 1458 as part of an alliance against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. She kept her <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-orthodox-church">Orthodox</a> Christian faith at his court, and her family ties helped link Uzun Hasan with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. Her daughter Halima was the mother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismail-i">Ismail I</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/safavid-empire">Safavid dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodora-megale-komnene.jpg" alt="Theodora Megale Komnene" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pisanello · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pisanello_011.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
